{
  "requirement": "The enabled Habeas Symposium plugin MUST request a global Cargo installation of the `habeas` CLI and use that installation as its session-start hook command, so the CLI is available when the hook advises an agent to run `habeas setup`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The requirement text has two structural obligations. Both are met by the `Cargo.toml` Symposium metadata.\n\n1. \"request a global Cargo installation of the `habeas` CLI\". The `[[package.metadata.symposium.installations]]` entry in `Cargo.toml` (`table[package.metadata.symposium.installations]`) declares this through four pairs. `pair[name]` is `habeas`, `pair[source]` is `cargo`, `pair[crate]` is `habeas`, and `pair[global]` is `true`. An alternative that leaves out the installation entry, uses a non-cargo source, or sets `global = false` would break the clause. All four pairs are marked `{impl}` roots.\n\n2. \"use that installation as its session-start hook command\". The `[[package.metadata.symposium.hooks]]` entry (`table[package.metadata.symposium.hooks]`) has `pair[command]` set to `habeas`, the installed executable, and `pair[name]` set to `habeas-setup-check`. The hook's `event` and `format` pairs, and the advice to run `habeas setup`, belong to `requirements.integration.symposium_setup_hook`. They are not needed here. The `executable` and `args` pairs and the hook `name` identifier are details the text does not constrain.\n\nThe `{impl}` markers on the six roots cover these obligations. No other source is needed, because the requirement is met entirely by declarative metadata in this file.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement has two behavioral obligations. The first is that the plugin requests a global Cargo installation of the `habeas` CLI. The second is that the session-start hook uses that installation as its command. Both are checked by `tests/repository.rs#fn[symposium_plugin_installs_the_cli_globally_for_its_session_start_hook]`, which parses the repository `Cargo.toml` through `repository_toml`.\n\n- **Installation:** The test asserts there is exactly one installation. It asserts `source == \"cargo\"`, `crate == \"habeas\"`, `executable == \"habeas\"` and `global == true`.\n- **Hook:** The test asserts there is exactly one hook, with event `SessionStart`. It asserts the hook `command` equals the installation's `executable`, so the hook uses the installed CLI. It also asserts the args are `hook session-start`.\n\nI see no untested clause or boundary. The \"enabled\" qualifier only describes the plugin being active. The plugin has no separate enable toggle in `Cargo.toml` that would need its own test. What the hook advises (`habeas setup`) is covered by the separate `symposium_setup_hook` requirement, not this one.",
  "references": "a6c4f0e64a68bbc6401b55bf90de985d33452cf5264c17d707356e164d24e9dc",
