        "rationale": "The requirement has two behavioral obligations. The first is that the plugin requests a global Cargo installation of the `habeas` CLI. The second is that the session-start hook uses that installation as its command. Both are checked by `tests/repository.rs#fn[symposium_plugin_installs_the_cli_globally_for_its_session_start_hook]`, which parses the repository `Cargo.toml` through `repository_toml`.\n\n- **Installation:** The test asserts there is exactly one installation. It asserts `source == \"cargo\"`, `crate == \"habeas\"`, `executable == \"habeas\"` and `global == true`.\n- **Hook:** The test asserts there is exactly one hook, with event `SessionStart`. It asserts the hook `command` equals the installation's `executable`, so the hook uses the installed CLI. It also asserts the args are `hook session-start`.\n\nI see no untested clause or boundary. The \"enabled\" qualifier only describes the plugin being active. The plugin has no separate enable toggle in `Cargo.toml` that would need its own test. What the hook advises (`habeas setup`) is covered by the separate `symposium_setup_hook` requirement, not this one."
